---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';

const principles = [
  {
    code: '01',
    title: 'Build before you preach.',
    body: 'A working project is a stronger argument than a claim about what a tool might make possible.',
  },
  {
    code: '02',
    title: 'AI amplifies judgement. It does not replace it.',
    body: 'Models can accelerate implementation, research and exploration. Intent, standards and responsibility still belong to the person directing the work.',
  },
  {
    code: '03',
    title: 'Test what can be tested.',
    body: 'A convincing output is not automatically a correct one. Software should run, rules should survive play and workflows should be checked against real use.',
  },
  {
    code: '04',
    title: 'Treat failures as evidence.',
    body: 'Broken builds, weak ideas and bad iterations are not wasted if they reveal what the process failed to understand.',
  },
  {
    code: '05',
    title: 'Learn while building.',
    body: 'Capability does not need to arrive fully formed before a project begins. Real problems can become the curriculum.',
  },
  {
    code: '06',
    title: 'Keep the human decisions visible.',
    body: 'Choosing, correcting, rejecting, verifying and deciding what deserves to survive are part of the work, not inconvenient steps to automate away.',
  },
  {
    code: '07',
    title: 'A prompt is not a process.',
    body: 'Useful results come from context, constraints, iteration, inspection and feedback loops. Prompting is one instrument inside a larger method.',
  },
  {
    code: '08',
    title: 'Access to capability matters.',
    body: 'New tools can let individuals attempt work that previously demanded larger teams, more specialised knowledge or resources they could not reach.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Manifesto"
  description="GVibeDev manifesto: AI is leverage, not autopilot. Build, test, verify, learn and keep human responsibility visible."
>
  <div class="manifesto-page">
    <section class="manifesto-hero">
      <Container>
        <span class="manifesto-code">// MANIFESTO_FULL</span>
        <div class="manifesto-hero__copy">
          <h1>AI is leverage,<br />not autopilot.</h1>
          <p>
            GVibeDev is built around a practical proposition: new tools can expand what one person
            is able to attempt, but capability only becomes useful when it is paired with judgement,
            method and responsibility.
          </p>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto-intro section-block">
      <Container>
        <div class="split">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">The position</span>
            <h2>The tool is not the author of the intention.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              A language model can help write code, reorganise a document, inspect a system,
              compare alternatives, produce a prototype or expose a path that would have taken much
              longer to reach alone.
            </p>
            <p>
              None of that transfers responsibility to the model. The direction of the work, the
              acceptance criteria, the decision to trust or reject an output and the consequences of
              publishing or using it remain human.
            </p>
            <p>
              That is why the interesting question is not whether AI can produce something. The
              interesting question is whether a person can build a process around the tool that
              produces something worth keeping.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="principles section-block">
      <Container>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <span class="eyebrow">Working principles</span>
          <h2>Method matters more as the tools become more powerful.</h2>
          <p>
            These are not rules for everyone. They are the working principles behind the projects
            collected on this site.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle-grid">
          {principles.map((principle) => (
            <article>
              <span>{principle.code}</span>
              <h3>{principle.title}</h3>
              <p>{principle.body}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="practice section-block">
      <Container>
        <div class="split">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">In practice</span>
            <h2>Generation is cheap. Acceptance is expensive.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              The visible output is often the fastest part of the process. The slower work is deciding
              what the project actually needs, noticing when the implementation has drifted, reproducing
              a failure, comparing alternatives and making a result stable enough to become a baseline.
            </p>
            <p>
              That pattern appears across the workshop: game rules are tested through matches,
              software through builds and regression checks, visual pipelines through repeated exports,
              and writing through structure, revision and comparison.
            </p>
            <blockquote>
              Speed is useful when it shortens the distance between a hypothesis and the evidence that
              can prove it wrong.
            </blockquote>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="responsibility section-block">
      <Container>
        <div class="split">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Responsibility</span>
            <h2>Power without discipline only accelerates error.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              Generative systems can also amplify weak research, false confidence, manipulation,
              shallow content and plausible mistakes. Better output quality does not remove the need
              to question the source, verify the claim or understand the context in which a result
              will be used.
            </p>
            <p>
              GVibeDev therefore treats AI assistance as part of an accountable workflow rather than
              an excuse to hide the human decisions behind the result.
            </p>
            <p>
              The goal is not to make the person disappear. The goal is to let the person reach further
              without pretending that reach and judgement are the same thing.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="evidence section-block">
      <Container>
        <div class="evidence-card">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">The archive is the argument</span>
            <h2>Build something, then show the work.</h2>
            <p>
              Games, tools, a novel, production workflows and a manual about working with language
              models all grew from the same approach: define the problem, use the available tools,
              inspect the result and keep iterating.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-actions">
            <a href="/projects/" class="button button--primary">Explore projects</a>
            <a href="/projects/manuale-llm/" class="button button--secondary">Manuale LLM</a>
            <a href="/about/" class="button button--secondary">About GVibeDev</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .manifesto-page { color: var(--color-text); background: var(--color-bg); }
  .section-block { padding-block: var(--section-space); }
  .eyebrow, .manifesto-code {
    color: var(--color-red-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .manifesto-hero {
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 8rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 8% 20%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-red) 13%, transparent), transparent 34%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 90% 80%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-blue) 15%, transparent), transparent 40%),
      var(--color-bg-deep);
  }
  .manifesto-hero :global(.container) { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .manifesto-hero__copy { display: grid; gap: 1.4rem; max-width: 65rem; }
  .manifesto-hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 12ch;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
    line-height: .9;
    letter-spacing: -.07em;
  }
  .manifesto-hero p, .section-heading > p, .prose p, .evidence-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .manifesto-hero p {
    max-width: 58rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1rem + .35vw, 1.35rem);
  }
  .split { display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
  .split > div:first-child, .section-heading, .prose { display: grid; gap: 1rem; align-content: start; }
  .split h2, .section-heading h2, .evidence-card h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.8vw, 4.4rem);
    line-height: .98;
    letter-spacing: -.05em;
  }
  .manifesto-intro, .responsibility { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .principles, .practice { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg-deep); }
  .section-heading { max-width: 60rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .principle-grid { display: grid; gap: 1px; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-border); }
  .principle-grid article {
    display: grid;
    gap: .7rem;
    padding: 1.1rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-1);
  }
  .principle-grid article > span {
    color: var(--color-blue-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .68rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .principle-grid h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .principle-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .prose blockquote {
    margin: .4rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-red-soft);
    color: var(--color-text);
    background: var(--color-surface-1);
    font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .evidence { background: var(--color-bg-deep); }
  .evidence-card {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    background: var(--color-surface-1);
  }
  .evidence-card > div:first-child { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .evidence-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; align-items: center; }
  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 2.8rem;
    padding: .8rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    color: var(--color-text);
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .045em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .button--primary {
    color: #08111e;
    background: var(--color-blue-soft);
    border-color: var(--color-blue-soft);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .principle-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }

  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .split { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: 4rem; }
    .principle-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .evidence-card { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(18rem, .8fr); gap: 4rem; align-items: center; }
    .evidence-actions { justify-content: flex-end; }
  }
</style>
